	(text "JACK DETECT (Workshop System Computer): PROBE drives a pseudo-random bit through a resistor to each input's\nswitch (normal) lug. Unpatched, the jack follows the sequence; patched, the lug opens. 100 kΩ for CV and audio\ninputs; 22 kΩ for gate inputs, whose 1.98 V threshold a 100 kΩ probe cannot reach (it gives ≈1.24 V)."
